2.1.text:
Article 8
The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 6 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.
The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
providing protection to women and children from acts of violence, in the form of establishing rules and regulations in their respective areas starting from the Neighborhood Association level;
providing information and or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties;
participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence; and accompanying victims to service units.
The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with laws and regulations.

Article 7
The obligations and responsibilities of Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include: establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; and allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity. ;
The duties of Regional Government in the protection of women and children from acts of violence in the form of: Implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
Collecting data and information about women and children in the context of efforts to protect from acts of violence;
Conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; and Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Article 11
Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 10, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of: social;
health;
education;
manpower;
women's empowerment and child protection;
mental and spiritual; and peace and order.
Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner.

CHAPTER VI
SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 12
Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, as follows: complaint services;
Medical services; and medicolegal services for the purpose of evidence in the field of law.
Legal aid services: independence or empowerment services; and social rehabilitation services.
Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented by related SKPD in accordance with the programs, activities, and budget available in each in the fields of: social;
health;
women's empowerment and child protection;
mental and spiritual;
employment; and education.

